# MageRide — ignored paths. Extended by C001 (repo-scaffold).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .NET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
*.user
*.suo
artifacts/
TestResults/
*.trx
*.coverage
*.coverisxml
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
msbuild.log
msbuild.err
.dotnet/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / Next.js (portals)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
.turbo/
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo
.eslintcache
coverage/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-store/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradle / Android / KMP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gradle/
build/
# ...but the top-level build/ is the MageRide build plan (manifest, prompts, progress),
# not a Gradle output directory.
!/build/
# C001 redirects the root project's buildDir to .gradle/root-build, but that override only
# takes effect once the root project is evaluated. A configuration failure earlier than that
# (a build-script compile error, for example) still drops Gradle's problems report into the
# default location — which is the build plan. Re-ignore the directories Gradle owns so a
# stray report can never be committed alongside the manifest. (C011)
/build/reports/
/build/tmp/
/build/kotlin/
# Same reasoning, different tool: ci.yml's iOS leg archives to `build/<scheme>.xcarchive`, and so
# does the Mac session that runs it by hand. That path is inside the un-ignored build plan, so
# without this an archive lands beside the manifest — several hundred megabytes of app binary and
# dSYM, in the directory the whole build is planned from.
/build/*.xcarchive/
# The Gradle wrapper is committed on purpose — never add a blanket *.jar rule above it.
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
local.properties
.kotlin/
.cxx/
captures/
*.hprof
*.klib
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# iOS / Xcode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
Pods/
.swiftpm/
Carthage/Build/
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets, keys and local environment
# `.env.*.example` templates (D7 §4, created by C009) stay tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example
!*.example
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
*.pem
# Δ C127: `*.key` was the one extension missing from this list, so an `openssl genrsa -out
# jwt-signing.key` — the exact command docs/runbooks/secret-rotation.md §1 tells an operator to
# run — produced a file `git add .` would have staged.
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.*.json
# Self-signed dev TLS material generated by infra/scripts/dev-up.sh for HAProxy (C009).
infra/deploy/certs/
# The device CA dev-up.sh generates for the hardware-tracker plane (C030, T-02). Its root
# key mints a working credential for any vehicle, so it never goes in the repository — EMQX
# and provisioning-svc both mount the directory instead.
infra/deploy/device-ca/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The GTFS feed, and the day-0 run's record (C126)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The feed is an EXTERNALLY PROVIDED file (AL-56) — a third-party dataset of tens of megabytes,
# whose distribution channel is its provider and not this repository. `gtfs-day0-load.sh` reads
# whatever is dropped here; nothing in the build depends on it being present.
infra/replica/gtfs/
# What one day-0 run observed on one deployment: timings, row counts, corridor answers. Evidence
# about a box, not a description of the platform — the transcribed record lives in
# docs/runbooks/gtfs-day0-load.md.
infra/replica/gtfs-day0-journal.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The load and capacity suite (C129)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# env.json carries EMQX's shared MQTT secret and a dozen live 30-minute bearers. It is written
# by load/configure.sh at 0600 and is never a template — there is nothing in it a second
# deployment could reuse.
load/env.json
# Raw run output: k6 summaries, container samples, before/after row counts. Evidence about one
# box on one afternoon; the transcribed figures live in load/report.md, which IS committed.
# (`out/` is already matched by the Node rule above — named here so the intent is not an
# accident of where a Next.js build happens to put its files.)
load/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The chaos drill suite (C130)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same shape and the same reasons as load/'s two entries above: env.json carries EMQX's shared
# MQTT secret plus live 30-minute bearers AND the opaque refresh tokens the Redis drill probes
# with, written at 0600 by chaos/configure.sh.
chaos/env.json
# One run's report and its raw samples. `chaos/run-drills.sh --report chaos/out/report.md` is
# the manifest's verify command, so this directory is written on every run; the transcribed
# findings live in chaos/report.md, which IS committed.
chaos/out/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vs/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db

# --- C131 acceptance/sg -------------------------------------------------------------
# Same shape and the same reasons as load/'s and chaos/'s entries above. env.json carries the
# TURN shared secret, a live bearer and the MQTT credential the downlink probe publishes with;
# it is written at 0600 by acceptance/sg/configure.sh and is never a template.
acceptance/sg/env.json
# One run's raw JSON and its generated report — a snapshot of one region on one afternoon,
# and every figure in it is region-specific by construction. The findings and the transcribed
# numbers live in acceptance/sg/report.md, which IS committed.
acceptance/sg/out/
# Deployment secrets and the TLS material for 5349, written on the target by
# infra/sg/deploy-media-sg.sh and never here.
infra/sg/secrets/
infra/sg/certs/
infra/sg/.env
